  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HO-TROSA2_BRASWaters proposal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will focus on developing the follow up phase of the Transboundary Rivers of South Asia (TROSA) program for the period 2023-2027 (tentative title: Building Resilience Across Shared Waters (BRASWaters). During this period key themes, focus areas and implementation approaches proposed for the BRASWaters program will be discussed with CO, current and new partners. These will build onthe insights and results from the TROSA program, the findings and recommendations from the evaluations (mid-term and end of program), and discussions with current TROSA partners during the Annual Learning Forum (held between 05 and 06 May 2022 in Kathmandu). These elements will be further discussed, revised and agreed upon in the process of developing a full proposal that will be submitted tothe donor. A key component of this process is a F2F meeting with (potential) partners to develop key elements of the proposal.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OXFAM International</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib was founded in 1956 as the Netherlands Organisation for International Assistance (Novib), and joined forces with Oxfam in 1994.  Oxfam Novib is member of the Oxfam International confederation. Working together in the confederation, the Oxfam affiliates can speak with one clear and compelling voice on issues of global concern: climate change, health and education for all, agriculture, trade, and conflicts and emergencies.  Oxfam Novib&apos;s main office is based in The Netherlands, it supports the work of a network of local offices, the implementation of global projects, fundraising, campaigning and advocacy.  Oxfam Novib&#x92;s the Hague office contributes towards this project&#x92;s implementation.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib</narrative>
